{"name":"Glow","hex":"#f9f2da","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"glow","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To emit heat and light without a flame.","To emit heat and light without a flame."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A state of heat and light being emitted by a hot object.","A state of heat being emitted by a person or an animal's body."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/glow"}],"entries":[{"title":"Glow (JavaScript library)","blocks":[{"text":"Glow is an open-source JavaScript library created by the BBC. Development on Glow began in 2007, and it was publicly released under an Apache License in July 2009."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/0/06/Glow_logo.png/330px-Glow_logo.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glow_(JavaScript_library)","wikidata":"Q5572214"},{"title":"Glow (Scottish Schools National Intranet)","blocks":[{"text":"Glow is the Scottish Schools National Intranet. It is a major national ICT and telecommunications programme managed by Education Scotland. The project is funded by the Scottish Government and is a collaboration between local authorities, Education Scotland and RM Education. The online portal is powered by RM Unify, a service which provides account management and the Launchpad, an interface which allows users to access applications provided by the Scottish Government, local authorities, and individual schools."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glow_(Scottish_Schools_National_Intranet)","wikidata":"Q5572221"},{"title":"GLOW (TV series)","blocks":[{"text":"GLOW is an American comedy-drama television series created by Liz Flahive and Carly Mensch for Netflix. The series revolves around a fictionalization of the characters and gimmicks of the 1980s syndicated women's professional wrestling circuit Gorgeous Ladies of Wrestling founded by David McLane."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki